 Use a **separate state** outside the repository, for example a dedicated protected working copy plus `TF_DATA_DIR` and an explicit local-state path. `TF_DATA_DIR` alone does not relocate state. Never copy the main course state or use the same backend key. The bootstrap is the sole owner of this account-wide budget. Keep the main course input `enable_budget_resource=false`; its currently authored monthly/tag-filtered foundation budget is not this cumulative monitor. A later migration requires an explicitly reviewed state/ownership procedure. Do not enable both roots for the same budget, import ad hoc, or delete an existing monitor to avoid a name conflict. `prevent_destroy=true` protects this monitor from routine cleanup; changing that protection requires its own human decision.
 
-Before deployment, the separate non-root execution identity needs budget creation/update/read/subscriber/notification permissions restricted to the proposed account budget ARN as supported by AWS, plus applicable tag permissions if used. Its policy must be reviewed from current AWS action/resource support. No IAM user, role, policy, attachment or broad administrator grant is authored or installed here. `scholarchain-planner` stays read-only. This bootstrap creates no report subscription, automated Budget Action, SNS topic or paid hourly cost data collection.
+Before deployment, the separate non-root execution identity requires tagging permissions because this root always supplies the five resource tags. AWS maps the `CreateBudget` API to `budgets:ModifyBudget`; creating a tagged budget also requires `budgets:TagResource`. Refresh and tag readback require `budgets:ViewBudget` and `budgets:ListTagsForResource`; tag changes require `budgets:TagResource`, with `budgets:UntagResource` for removals. Review these IAM actions against the exact proposed budget ARN and the current [AWS Budget Service authorization reference](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_budgets.html) (checked 2026-10-31); API operation names are not interchangeable with IAM action names. No permission is granted by this documentation. No IAM user, role, policy, attachment or broad administrator grant is authored or installed here. `scholarchain-planner` stays read-only. This bootstrap creates no report subscription, automated Budget Action, SNS topic or paid hourly cost data collection.
